+		AddTouch( "_spec_spec_1", "spec_mode 1; _spec_toggle_menu_spectate_options", SpecMenu::MenuItem( l, m, 5 ));
 	}
 	else
 	{
diff --git a/cl_dll/hud/spectator_layout.h b/cl_dll/hud/spectator_layout.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..708aa26
--- /dev/null
+++ b/cl_dll/hud/spectator_layout.h
@@ -0,0 +1,272 @@
+//
+// spectator_layout.h
+//
+// The upper bar of the spectator mode as in the Steam version of CS 1.6, measured on its screenshots
+// (1920x1080 and 1600x900). Its sizes are in units of 1/480 of the screen height ("proportional" sizes
+// of VGUI2) and the elements are placed from the right edge of the screen:
+//
+//   Counter-Terrorists :  0  |  $800
+//          Terrorists :  0  |  (timer) 1:45
+//
+// No dependencies on the engine, so it can be tested alone.
+//
+
+#pragma once
+
+namespace SpecBar {
+
+// One unit in pixels
+inline float Unit( int screenH )
+{
+	return screenH / 480.0f;
+}
+
+// Height of the black bars (64 units, 144 pixels at 1080)
+inline int BarHeight( int screenH )
+{
+	return int( screenH * 64 / 480 );
+}
+
+// The font of the bar is "Default" of resource/ClientScheme.res (Verdana, weight 600): its size depends
+// on the height of the screen; the Steam version draws a "tall" of the scheme with letters of tall * 3 / 4 pixels
+// (rounded down): 20 -> 15 at 1080 (capitals of 11 pixels, small letters of 8), 14 -> 10 for the tutor
+struct Font
+{
+	int tall;
+	bool antialias;
+};
+
+inline Font FontFor( int screenH )
+{
+	if( screenH < 600 )  return { 12, false };
+	if( screenH < 768 )  return { 13, false };
+	if( screenH < 1024 ) return { 14, true };
+	if( screenH < 1200 ) return { 20, true };
+	return { 24, true };
+}
+
+inline int FontEm( int tall )
+{
+	const int em = tall * 3 / 4;
+	return em < 4 ? 4 : em;
+}
+
+// The top of the capitals of the two rows (38 and 65 of 1080) and their distance from the top of the cell
+// of the font (the ascent of Verdana is 1.005 em, its capitals are 0.727 em high)
+inline float Row1CapTop( int screenH ) { return 16.9f * Unit( screenH ); }
+inline float Row2CapTop( int screenH ) { return 28.9f * Unit( screenH ); }
+inline int CellTopFromCapTop( float capTop, int em ) { return int( capTop - 0.278f * em + 0.5f ); }
+
+struct Layout
+{
+	int teamLabelRight;  // right edge of "Counter-Terrorists :" and "Terrorists :" (right aligned)
+	int teamValueX;      // left edge of the scores
+	int dividerX, dividerY, dividerW, dividerH; // the vertical line
+	int infoX;           // left edge of the money (or the map name) in the first row
+	int timerIconX, timerIconY, timerIconSize;
+	int timerTextX;      // left edge of the time in the second row
+};
+
+inline Layout Compute( int screenW, int screenH )
+{
+	const float u = Unit( screenH );
+	auto fromRight = [screenW, u]( float units ) { return int( screenW - units * u + 0.5f ); };
+
+	Layout l;
+	l.teamLabelRight = fromRight( 83.1f );  // ':' ends at 1729 of 1920
+	l.teamValueX = fromRight( 80.0f );      // "0" at 1741
+	l.dividerX = fromRight( 64.0f );        // 1776..1777
+	l.dividerW = int( u + 0.5f ) > 0 ? int( u + 0.5f ) : 1;
+	l.dividerY = int( 12.0f * u + 0.5f );   // 27..93
+	l.dividerH = int( 30.0f * u + 0.5f ) - 1;
+	l.infoX = fromRight( 56.0f );           // "$" at 1795
+	l.timerIconX = fromRight( 56.0f );      // the picture of the icon is seen at 1798..1814 x 59..81
+	l.timerIconY = int( 25.3f * u + 0.5f );
+	l.timerIconSize = int( 12.4f * u + 0.5f );
+	l.timerTextX = fromRight( 41.7f );      // 1826: "0:00" is seen at 1827..1865 (1 pixel of bearing)
+	return l;
+}
+
+} // namespace SpecBar
+
+// The menus of the spectator mode as in the Steam version (measured on its screenshots at 1920x1080):
+//   at the bottom: "Options" 11..313, the previous player 567..611, the player 623..1297 (in the middle of the
+//   screen), the next player 1308..1352, the camera mode 1605..1907, all of them 1003..1051 (frames of 1 pixel,
+//   "BorderBright"); the lists have a small grey arrow on the right, the buttons orange triangles
+//   a menu opens above its list (its frame ends 2 pixels above it) and is as wide; its items are 66 pixels high,
+//   the text in "DefaultSmall" (Verdana, thin) with its capitals in the middle of the item, 31 pixels from the
+//   edge if the menu has check marks (they are at 15), else 7; an open submenu is lit (255 176 0, 48 %)
+namespace SpecMenu {
+
+struct Rect
+{
+	int x = 0, y = 0, w = 0, h = 0;
+};
+
+struct Layout
+{
+	float u = 1.0f;
+	Rect options, prev, player, next, view; // the controls at the bottom
+	int itemH = 0;                          // an item of a menu
+	int comboTextInset = 0, comboCapTop = 0;
+	int menuTextInset = 0, menuCheckTextInset = 0, menuCheckX = 0;
+
+	int U( float v ) const { return int( v * u + 0.5f ); }
+};
+
+inline Layout Compute( int screenW, int screenH )
+{
+	Layout l;
+	l.u = screenH / 480.0f;
+
+	const int y = screenH - l.U( 34.2f );
+	const int h = l.U( 21.8f );
+	const int comboW = l.U( 134.7f );
+	const int buttonW = l.U( 20.0f );
+	const int mid = screenW / 2;
+
+	l.options = { l.U( 4.9f ), y, comboW, h };
+	l.prev    = { mid - l.U( 174.7f ), y, buttonW, h };
+	l.player  = { mid - l.U( 149.8f ), y, l.U( 300.0f ), h };
+	l.next    = { mid + l.U( 154.7f ), y, buttonW, h };
+	l.view    = { screenW - l.U( 140.0f ), y, comboW, h };
+
+	// a narrow screen (4:3, 5:4): the lists on the sides are made narrower to keep the gap of the Steam version
+	// (12 pixels at 1080) to the buttons in the middle
+	const int gap = l.U( 5.3f );
+	if( l.options.x + l.options.w > l.prev.x - gap )
+		l.options.w = l.prev.x - gap - l.options.x;
+	if( l.view.x < l.next.x + l.next.w + gap )
+	{
+		const int right = l.view.x + l.view.w;
+		l.view.x = l.next.x + l.next.w + gap;
+		l.view.w = right - l.view.x;
+	}
+
+	l.itemH = l.U( 29.33f );
+	l.comboTextInset = l.U( 1.3f );
+	l.comboCapTop = l.U( 8.0f );
+	l.menuTextInset = l.U( 3.1f );
+	l.menuCheckTextInset = l.U( 13.8f );
+	l.menuCheckX = l.U( 6.7f );
+	return l;
+}
+
+// The frame of a menu of "items" items opened above the list "combo"
+inline Rect MenuAbove( const Layout &l, const Rect &combo, int items )
+{
+	Rect r;
+	r.x = combo.x;
+	r.w = combo.w;
+	r.h = items * l.itemH + 2;
+	r.y = combo.y - 2 - ( r.h - 1 );
+	return r;
+}
+
+// The frame of a submenu opened to the right of the item "item" of the menu "menu"; width - its width (as wide
+// as its texts in the Steam version: "Settings" 315..501 at 1080), 0 - as wide as the menu
+inline Rect SubmenuRight( const Layout &l, const Rect &menu, int item, int items, int width = 0 )
+{
+	Rect r;
+	r.x = menu.x + menu.w;
+	r.w = width > 0 ? width : menu.w;
+	r.h = items * l.itemH + 2;
+	r.y = menu.y + item * l.itemH;
+	return r;
+}
+
+// The item i of a menu
+inline Rect MenuItem( const Layout &l, const Rect &menu, int i )
+{
+	Rect r;
+	r.x = menu.x + 1;
+	r.w = menu.w - 2;
+	r.y = menu.y + 1 + i * l.itemH;
+	r.h = l.itemH;
+	return r;
+}
+
+// The width of a menu with check marks for its widest text (textW): the text from menuCheckTextInset, 13 pixels
+// after it at 1080 (as the "Settings" submenu of the Steam version)
+inline int CheckMenuWidth( const Layout &l, int textW )
+{
+	return l.menuCheckTextInset + textW + l.U( 5.8f );
+}
+
+// The list of the players (it opens above the player): as the ComboBox of the Steam version it shows up to
+// 10 items at once, the others are reached with a scroll bar on its right side
+const int PLAYERS_VISIBLE = 10;
+
+// how many items are seen if there are "count" players (they are not higher than the space above the list)
+inline int PlayersVisible( const Layout &l, int count, int screenH, int barH )
+{
+	int n = count < PLAYERS_VISIBLE ? count : PLAYERS_VISIBLE;
+	const int room = ( l.player.y - 2 - barH - 2 ) / ( l.itemH > 0 ? l.itemH : 1 );
+	if( n > room )
+		n = room;
+	return n > 0 ? n : 0;
+}
+
+inline int ScrollBarWidth( const Layout &l )
+{
+	return l.U( 23.1f ); // 52 at 1080: 1244..1295 inside the frame of the list 623..1297
+}
+
+inline int ScrollButtonHeight( const Layout &l )
+{
+	return l.U( 23.6f ); // 53 at 1080: 342..394
+}
+
+// the scroll bar inside the frame of the menu; its buttons are squares at its ends
+inline Rect ScrollBar( const Layout &l, const Rect &menu )
+{
+	Rect r;
+	r.w = ScrollBarWidth( l );
+	r.x = menu.x + menu.w - 1 - r.w;
+	r.y = menu.y + 1;
+	r.h = menu.h - 2;
+	return r;
+}
+
+inline Rect ScrollUp( const Layout &l, const Rect &menu )
+{
+	Rect r = ScrollBar( l, menu );
+	r.h = ScrollButtonHeight( l );
+	return r;
+}
+
+inline Rect ScrollDown( const Layout &l, const Rect &menu )
+{
+	Rect r = ScrollBar( l, menu );
+	r.h = ScrollButtonHeight( l );
+	r.y = menu.y + menu.h - 1 - r.h;
+	return r;
+}
+
+// the thumb of the scroll bar: "first" - the first item seen, "visible" of "count"
+inline Rect ScrollThumb( const Layout &l, const Rect &menu, int first, int visible, int count )
+{
+	// at 1080 with 10 of 15 players: the thumb 396..763 between the buttons 342..394 and 948..1000
+	const Rect bar = ScrollBar( l, menu );
+	const int bh = ScrollButtonHeight( l );
+	Rect r = bar;
+	const int track = bar.h - bh * 2;
+	if( count <= visible || track <= 0 )
+	{
+		r.y = bar.y + bh;
+		r.h = track > 0 ? track : 0;
+		return r;
+	}
+	int h = track * visible / count;
+	const int minH = bh < track ? bh : track;
+	if( h < minH )
+		h = minH;
+	if( h > track )
+		h = track;
+	const int maxFirst = count - visible;
+	r.y = bar.y + bh + ( track - h ) * first / maxFirst;
+	r.h = h;
+	return r;
+}
+
+} // namespace SpecMenu
diff --git a/cl_dll/hud/text_texture.cpp b/cl_dll/hud/text_texture.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b7a5163
--- /dev/null
+++ b/cl_dll/hud/text_texture.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,274 @@
+//
+// text_texture.cpp
+//
+
+#include "hud.h"
+#include "cl_util.h"
+#include "triangleapi.h"
+#include "draw_util.h"
+
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <string.h>
+#include <ctype.h>
+#include <math.h>
+#include <vector>
+
+#include "text_texture.h"
+#include "glyph_atlas.h"
+#include "client_texture.h"
+
+void CTextTexture::Free()
+{
+	m_pFont = nullptr;
+	m_quads.clear();
+	m_iWidth = m_iHeight = 0;
+	m_bFailed = false;
+	m_key.clear();
+}
+
+int CTextTexture::Ascent() const
+{
+	return m_pFont ? m_pFont->Ascent() : 0;
+}
+
+bool CTextTexture::Update( const std::string &utf8, const char *fontName, int emHeight, int weight, bool antialias,
+						   int maxWidth, bool ellipsis )
+{
+	if( maxWidth < 8 )
+		maxWidth = 8;
+
+	char extra[128];
+	snprintf( extra, sizeof( extra ), "|%s|%d|%d|%d|%d|%d", fontName ? fontName : "", emHeight, weight,
+		antialias ? 1 : 0, maxWidth, ellipsis ? 1 : 0 );
+	const std::string key = utf8 + extra;
+
+	if( key == m_key )
+		return !m_bFailed;
+
+	Free();
+	m_key = key;
+
+	CGlyphFont *font = CGlyphFont::Get( fontName, emHeight, weight, antialias );
+	if( !font )
+	{
+		m_bFailed = true;
+		return false;
+	}
+
+	m_pFont = font;
+
+	if( utf8.empty() )
+		return true; // nothing to draw
+
+	std::u32string text = GlyphText_Decode( utf8 );
+	font->Prepare( text );
+	if( ellipsis )
+		font->Prepare( U"." );
+
+	auto advanceOf = [font]( char32_t c ) {
+		const CGlyphFont::Glyph *g = font->Find( c );
+		return g ? g->advance : 0;
+	};
+
+	// the lines
+	std::vector<std::u32string> lines( 1 );
+	for( char32_t c : text )
+	{
+		if( c == '\n' )
+			lines.emplace_back();
+		else if( c != '\r' )
+			lines.back().push_back( c );
+	}
+
+	const int lineH = font->Height();
+	const int tab = font->TabWidth();
+
+	for( size_t li = 0; li < lines.size(); ++li )
+	{
+		std::u32string &line = lines[li];
+
+		// the pen positions of the letters (the tabs go to the next stop, as DT_EXPANDTABS)
+		auto measure = [&]( const std::u32string &s ) {
+			int pen = 0;
+			for( char32_t c : s )
+				pen = ( c == '\t' ) ? ( pen / tab + 1 ) * tab : pen + advanceOf( c );
+			return pen;
+		};
+
+		// too wide with "...": letters are taken away until it fits (as DT_END_ELLIPSIS)
+		if( ellipsis && measure( line ) > maxWidth )
+		{
+			const int dots = advanceOf( '.' ) * 3;
+			while( !line.empty() && measure( line ) + dots > maxWidth )
+				line.pop_back();
+			line += U"...";
+		}
+
+		int pen = 0;
+		const int top = (int)li * lineH;
+
+		for( char32_t c : line )
+		{
+			if( c == '\t' )
+			{
+				pen = ( pen / tab + 1 ) * tab;
+				continue;
+			}
+
+			const CGlyphFont::Glyph *g = font->Find( c );
+			if( !g )
+				g = font->Find( '?' );
+			if( !g )
+				continue;
+
+			if( g->page >= 0 )
+			{
+				Quad q;
+				q.page = g->page;
+				q.x = pen + g->left;
+				q.y = top;
+				q.w = g->w;
+				q.h = g->h;
+				q.sx = g->x;
+				q.sy = g->y;
+
+				// the picture is cut at the edges of the text (as the old picture of the whole text was)
+				if( q.x < 0 )
+				{
+					q.sx -= q.x;
+					q.w += q.x;
+					q.x = 0;
+				}
+				if( q.x + q.w > maxWidth )
+					q.w = maxWidth - q.x;
+
+				if( q.w > 0 )
+					m_quads.push_back( q );
+			}
+
+			pen += g->advance;
+		}
+
+		const int w = pen < maxWidth ? pen : maxWidth;
+		if( w > m_iWidth )
+			m_iWidth = w;
+	}
+
+	m_iHeight = (int)lines.size() * lineH;
+	return true;
+}
+
+void CTextTexture::Draw( float x, float y, int r, int g, int b, int a ) const
+{
+	if( !m_pFont || m_quads.empty() )
+		return;
+
+	// whole pixels: every texel of the atlas lands on its own pixel
+	const int ox = (int)floorf( x + 0.5f );
+	const int oy = (int)floorf( y + 0.5f );
+
+	gRenderAPI.GL_SelectTexture( 0 );
+	gEngfuncs.pTriAPI->RenderMode( kRenderTransAlpha );
+	gEngfuncs.pTriAPI->Color4f( r / 255.0f, g / 255.0f, b / 255.0f, a / 255.0f );
+
+	// the letters of every page together (a text has almost always one page)
+	std::vector<int> pages;
+
+	for( const Quad &q : m_quads )
+	{
+		bool seen = false;
+		for( int p : pages )
+			seen = seen || p == q.page;
+		if( !seen )
+			pages.push_back( q.page );
+	}
+
+	for( int p : pages )
+	{
+		const int tex = m_pFont->PageTexture( p );
+		if( tex <= 0 )
+			continue;
+
+		const float pw = (float)m_pFont->PageWidth( p );
+		const float ph = (float)m_pFont->PageHeight( p );
+
+		gRenderAPI.GL_Bind( 0, tex );
+		gEngfuncs.pTriAPI->Begin( TRI_QUADS );
+
+		for( const Quad &q : m_quads )
+		{
+			if( q.page != p )
+				continue;
+
+			const float x1 = (float)( ox + q.x ), y1 = (float)( oy + q.y );
+			const float x2 = x1 + q.w, y2 = y1 + q.h;
+			const float s1 = q.sx / pw, t1 = q.sy / ph;
+			const float s2 = ( q.sx + q.w ) / pw, t2 = ( q.sy + q.h ) / ph;
+
+			gEngfuncs.pTriAPI->TexCoord2f( s1, t1 );
+			gEngfuncs.pTriAPI->Vertex3f( x1, y1, 0 );
+			gEngfuncs.pTriAPI->TexCoord2f( s1, t2 );
+			gEngfuncs.pTriAPI->Vertex3f( x1, y2, 0 );
+			gEngfuncs.pTriAPI->TexCoord2f( s2, t2 );
+			gEngfuncs.pTriAPI->Vertex3f( x2, y2, 0 );
+			gEngfuncs.pTriAPI->TexCoord2f( s2, t1 );
+			gEngfuncs.pTriAPI->Vertex3f( x2, y1, 0 );
+		}
+
+		gEngfuncs.pTriAPI->End();
+	}
+
+	gEngfuncs.pTriAPI->RenderMode( kRenderNormal );
+}
+
+// cl_textures_check: the textures of the fonts of the engine (the chat and the kill feed are drawn with them)
+// and how many textures the client has made. A font whose texture is missing here is drawn as black boxes.
+static void TextTexturesCheck( void )
+{
+	if( !gRenderAPI.GL_TextureName )
+	{
+		gEngfuncs.Con_Printf( "cl_textures_check: the engine does not tell the names of the textures\n" );
+		return;
+	}
+
+	int total = 0, glyphs = 0, chrome = 0;
+	const char *prefix = CGlyphFont::TexturePrefix();
+	const size_t prefixLen = strlen( prefix );
+
+	gEngfuncs.Con_Printf( "the textures of the fonts:\n" );
+	for( int i = 1; i < 8192; ++i )
+	{
+		const char *name = gRenderAPI.GL_TextureName( (unsigned int)i );
+		if( !name || !name[0] )
+			continue;
+
+		++total;
+		if( !strncmp( name, prefix, prefixLen )) ++glyphs;
+		else if( !strncmp( name, "*chrome_", 8 )) ++chrome;
+
+		char lower[256];
+		size_t n = 0;
+		for( ; name[n] && n + 1 < sizeof( lower ); ++n )
+			lower[n] = (char)tolower( (unsigned char)name[n] );
+		lower[n] = 0;
+
+		if( strstr( lower, "font" ) || strstr( lower, "conchars" ))
+		{
+			gEngfuncs.Con_Printf( "  %4d  %4d x %-4d  %s\n", i,
+				gRenderAPI.RenderGetParm ? gRenderAPI.RenderGetParm( PARM_TEX_WIDTH, i ) : 0,
+				gRenderAPI.RenderGetParm ? gRenderAPI.RenderGetParm( PARM_TEX_HEIGHT, i ) : 0, name );
+		}
+	}
+
+	gEngfuncs.Con_Printf( "all textures: %d; made by the client: pages of the font atlases %d, browser %d\n",
+		total, glyphs, chrome );
+	ClientTexture::PrintJournal( 64 );
+	gEngfuncs.Con_Printf( "con_fontsize %s, con_charset %s, cl_charset %s, hud_textmode %s\n",
+		gEngfuncs.pfnGetCvarString( "con_fontsize" ), gEngfuncs.pfnGetCvarString( "con_charset" ),
+		gEngfuncs.pfnGetCvarString( "cl_charset" ), gEngfuncs.pfnGetCvarString( "hud_textmode" ));
+}
+
+void TextTexture_RegisterCommands( void )
+{
+	gEngfuncs.pfnAddCommand( "cl_textures_check", TextTexturesCheck );
+}
diff --git a/cl_dll/hud/text_texture.h b/cl_dll/hud/text_texture.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f312f92
--- /dev/null
+++ b/cl_dll/hud/text_texture.h
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+//
+// text_texture.h
+//
+// A piece of text in a font of Windows, put together from the atlas of the font (glyph_atlas.h): a new text costs
+// no new texture. Used where the client draws text like the VGUI2 panels of the Steam version.
+//
+
+#pragma once
+
+#include <string>
+#include <vector>
+
+class CGlyphFont;
+
+// adds the command cl_textures_check (the textures of the fonts of the engine, see client_texture.h)
+void TextTexture_RegisterCommands( void );
+
+class CTextTexture
+{
+public:
+	// Lays the text out if something has changed. Returns false if the fonts of Windows are not available
+	// (then the caller draws the text with the font of the HUD). Line ends start new lines; a line wider than
+	// maxWidth pixels is cut there, or ends with "..." if ellipsis is set.
+	bool Update( const std::string &utf8, const char *fontName, int emHeight, int weight, bool antialias,
+				 int maxWidth = 4096, bool ellipsis = false );
+
+	// Draws the text with the top left corner of its cell at (x, y), in pixels of the screen
+	void Draw( float x, float y, int r, int g, int b, int a = 255 ) const;
+
+	void Free();
+
+	int Width() const { return m_iWidth; }   // the widest line (the advance of its letters)
+	int Height() const { return m_iHeight; } // the lines (the height of the font each)
+	int Ascent() const;                      // from the top of a line to its baseline
+	bool Valid() const { return m_pFont != nullptr; }
+
+private:
+	struct Quad
+	{
+		int page;
+		int x, y, w, h;   // on the screen, from the top left corner of the text
+		int sx, sy;       // in the page
+	};
+
+	CGlyphFont *m_pFont = nullptr;
+	std::vector<Quad> m_quads;
+	int m_iWidth = 0, m_iHeight = 0;
+	bool m_bFailed = false;
+	std::string m_key;
+};
diff --git a/cl_dll/hud/text_utf8.h b/cl_dll/hud/text_utf8.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7b712a8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/cl_dll/hud/text_utf8.h
@@ -0,0 +1,93 @@
+//
+// text_utf8.h
+//
+// Texts that come from servers are in UTF-8 or in the Windows-1251 code page (Russian servers).
+// Anything that is not valid UTF-8 is taken as Windows-1251 and converted to UTF-8.
+// No dependencies on the engine.
+//
+
+#pragma once
+
+#include <string>
+
+namespace TextUtf {
+
+inline bool IsValidUtf8( const char* s )
+{
+	const unsigned char* p = reinterpret_cast<const unsigned char*>( s );
+
+	while( *p )
+	{
+		int n;
+
+		if( *p < 0x80 )
+			n = 0;
+		else if(( *p & 0xE0 ) == 0xC0 && *p >= 0xC2 )
+			n = 1;
+		else if(( *p & 0xF0 ) == 0xE0 )
+			n = 2;
+		else if(( *p & 0xF8 ) == 0xF0 && *p <= 0xF4 )
+			n = 3;
+		else
+			return false;
+
+		for( int i = 1; i <= n; ++i )
+			if(( p[i] & 0xC0 ) != 0x80 )
+				return false;
+
+		p += n + 1;
+	}
+
+	return true;
+}
+
+inline void AppendUtf8( std::string& out, unsigned int cp )
+{
+	if( cp < 0x80 )
+	{
+		out += (char)cp;
+	}
+	else if( cp < 0x800 )
+	{
+		out += (char)( 0xC0 | ( cp >> 6 ));
+		out += (char)( 0x80 | ( cp & 0x3F ));
+	}
+	else
+	{
+		out += (char)( 0xE0 | ( cp >> 12 ));
+		out += (char)( 0x80 | (( cp >> 6 ) & 0x3F ));
+		out += (char)( 0x80 | ( cp & 0x3F ));
+	}
+}
+
+// Anything that is not valid UTF-8 is taken as Windows-1251
+inline std::string ToUtf8( const char* s )
+{
+	if( !s )
+		return std::string();
+
+	if( IsValidUtf8( s ))
+		return std::string( s );
+
+	static const unsigned short cp1251_80_BF[64] = {
+		0x0402, 0x0403, 0x201A, 0x0453, 0x201E, 0x2026, 0x2020, 0x2021, 0x20AC, 0x2030, 0x0409, 0x2039, 0x040A, 0x040C, 0x040B, 0x040F,
+		0x0452, 0x2018, 0x2019, 0x201C, 0x201D, 0x2022, 0x2013, 0x2014, 0xFFFD, 0x2122, 0x0459, 0x203A, 0x045A, 0x045C, 0x045B, 0x045F,
+		0x00A0, 0x040E, 0x045E, 0x0408, 0x00A4, 0x0490, 0x00A6, 0x00A7, 0x0401, 0x00A9, 0x0404, 0x00AB, 0x00AC, 0x00AD, 0x00AE, 0x0407,
+		0x00B0, 0x00B1, 0x0406, 0x0456, 0x0491, 0x00B5, 0x00B6, 0x00B7, 0x0451, 0x2116, 0x0454, 0x00BB, 0x0458, 0x0405, 0x0455, 0x0457 };
+
+	std::string out;
+
+	for( const unsigned char* p = reinterpret_cast<const unsigned char*>( s ); *p; ++p )
+	{
+		if( *p < 0x80 )
+			out += (char)*p;
+		else if( *p < 0xC0 )
+			AppendUtf8( out, cp1251_80_BF[*p - 0x80] );
+		else
+			AppendUtf8( out, 0x0410 + ( *p - 0xC0 )); // A..ya
+	}
+
+	return out;
+}
+
+} // namespace TextUtf
diff --git a/cl_dll/hud/texture_watch.cpp b/cl_dll/hud/texture_watch.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9783d90
--- /dev/null
+++ b/cl_dll/hud/texture_watch.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,182 @@
+//
+// texture_watch.cpp
+//
+// Looks for the cause of the black boxes instead of the texts of the chat and the kill feed: they appear when the
+// texture of a font of the engine is freed while the font still uses its number (then a texture of the map gets
+// that number). Every frame the textures of the fonts are found by their names; when one of them is gone, the
+// console gets a line about it and the journal of the last operations of the client with its own textures.
+// Run the game with -log to keep it all in engine.log.
+//
+
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <string.h>
+
+#include "hud.h"
+#include "cl_util.h"
+#include "client_texture.h"
+
+namespace ClientTexture {
+
+namespace {
+
+struct JournalEntry
+{
+	float time;
+	char op[24];
+	int tex;
+	char name[48];
+};
+
+const int JOURNAL_SIZE = 64;
+JournalEntry g_journal[JOURNAL_SIZE];
+int g_journalCount = 0; // all entries ever written
+
+float Now( void )
+{
+	return gEngfuncs.GetClientTime ? gEngfuncs.GetClientTime() : 0.0f;
+}
+
+struct WatchedFont
+{
+	char name[64];
+	int tex;
+	int conFont;   // the number of the console font (con_fontsize), -1 for the others
+	bool broken;   // its texture is gone while the font still uses its number
+};
+
+const int MAX_WATCHED = 12;
+WatchedFont g_watched[MAX_WATCHED];
+int g_watchedCount = 0;
+char g_watchedCharset[32] = "\x01"; // the names depend on con_charset
+bool g_fontBroken = false;
+
+void BuildWatchList( const char *charset )
+{
+	g_watchedCount = 0;
+	auto add = [charset]( const char *fmt, int i )
+	{
+		if( g_watchedCount >= MAX_WATCHED )
+			return;
+		WatchedFont &w = g_watched[g_watchedCount++];
+		snprintf( w.name, sizeof( w.name ), fmt, i, charset );
+		w.tex = 0;
+		w.conFont = i;
+		w.broken = false;
+	};
+
+	for( int i = 0; i < 3; ++i )
+		add( "font%d_%s.fnt", i );
+	for( int i = 0; i < 3; ++i )
+		add( "fonts/font%d", i );
+
+	const char *others[3] = { "creditsfont_%s.fnt", "gfx/creditsfont.fnt", "gfx/conchars" };
+	for( const char *fmt : others )
+	{
+		if( g_watchedCount >= MAX_WATCHED )
+			break;
+		WatchedFont &w = g_watched[g_watchedCount++];
+		snprintf( w.name, sizeof( w.name ), fmt, charset );
+		w.tex = 0;
+		w.conFont = -1;
+		w.broken = false;
+	}
+}
+
+} // namespace
+
+void Note( const char *op, int tex, const char *name )
+{
+	JournalEntry &e = g_journal[g_journalCount % JOURNAL_SIZE];
+	e.time = Now();
+	snprintf( e.op, sizeof( e.op ), "%s", op ? op : "" );
+	e.tex = tex;
+	snprintf( e.name, sizeof( e.name ), "%s", name ? name : "" );
+	++g_journalCount;
+}
+
+void PrintJournal( int count )
+{
+	if( count > JOURNAL_SIZE )
+		count = JOURNAL_SIZE;
+	if( count > g_journalCount )
+		count = g_journalCount;
+
+	gEngfuncs.Con_Printf( "[font watch] the last %d operations of the client with its textures (of %d):\n", count, g_journalCount );
+	for( int i = g_journalCount - count; i < g_journalCount; ++i )
+	{
+		const JournalEntry &e = g_journal[i % JOURNAL_SIZE];
+		gEngfuncs.Con_Printf( "  %9.2f  %-18s %5d  %s\n", e.time, e.op, e.tex, e.name );
+	}
+}
+
+void WatchFonts( void )
+{
+	if( !gRenderAPI.GL_FindTexture )
+		return;
+
+	const char *charset = gEngfuncs.pfnGetCvarString( "con_charset" );
+	if( !charset )
+		charset = "";
+
+	if( strcmp( charset, g_watchedCharset ))
+	{
+		snprintf( g_watchedCharset, sizeof( g_watchedCharset ), "%s", charset );
+		BuildWatchList( charset );
+	}
+
+	for( int i = 0; i < g_watchedCount; ++i )
+	{
+		WatchedFont &w = g_watched[i];
+		const int tex = gRenderAPI.GL_FindTexture( w.name );
+		if( tex == w.tex )
+			continue;
+
+		if( w.tex > 0 )
+		{
+			const char *now = gRenderAPI.GL_TextureName ? gRenderAPI.GL_TextureName( (unsigned int)w.tex ) : "";
+			char again[64] = "";
+			if( tex > 0 )
+				snprintf( again, sizeof( again ), " (its file is loaded again as number %d)", tex );
+			gEngfuncs.Con_Printf( "[font watch] the texture of the font \"%s\" (number %d) is gone at %.2f%s; "
+				"the number %d is now \"%s\"\n", w.name, w.tex, Now(), again, w.tex, now ? now : "" );
+			PrintJournal( 24 );
+
+			if( w.conFont >= 0 && tex <= 0 )
+			{
+				w.broken = true;
+				gEngfuncs.Con_Printf( "[font watch] the chat and the kill feed are drawn with the font of the HUD now "
+					"(as with hud_textmode 1)\n" );
+			}
+		}
+		else
+		{
+			gEngfuncs.Con_Printf( "[font watch] the font \"%s\" is texture number %d\n", w.name, tex );
+		}
+
+		if( tex > 0 )
+			w.broken = false; // the engine has loaded the font again
+
+		w.tex = tex;
+	}
+
+	// the console font the client uses (con_fontsize) is broken: found once a frame, used by every text
+	int size = (int)gEngfuncs.pfnGetCvarFloat( "con_fontsize" );
+	if( size < 0 )
+		size = 0;
+	if( size > 2 )
+		size = 2;
+
+	g_fontBroken = false;
+	for( int i = 0; i < g_watchedCount; ++i )
+	{
+		if( g_watched[i].broken && g_watched[i].conFont == size )
+			g_fontBroken = true;
+	}
+}
+
+bool EngineFontBroken( void )
+{
+	return g_fontBroken;
+}
+
+} // namespace ClientTexture
diff --git a/cl_dll/hud/tutor.cpp b/cl_dll/hud/tutor.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0158661
--- /dev/null
+++ b/cl_dll/hud/tutor.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,364 @@
+//
+// tutor.cpp
+//
+// Tutor messages of the server: TutorText shows a message in the upper right corner of the screen,
+// TutorClose hides it (TutorState and TutorLine are read and not used, as in the Steam version of CS 1.6).
+// They are sent by ReGameDLL (the tutor of Condition Zero) and by many AMX Mod X plugins.
+//
+// The window repeats the one of the Steam version (see tutor_logic.h for the sizes): one line of text,
+// the window gets as wide as the text is. Its colours and font
+// are taken from resource/TutorScheme.res (servers send this file with the plugins), the icons from
+// gfx/career/icon_i.tga and icon_skulls.tga. Without these files the window is drawn by the client itself.
+//
+// cl_tutor 0          - do not show the messages
+// cl_tutor_maxtime N  - hide a message after N seconds even if the server does not close it (0 - never)
+//
+
+#include "hud.h"
+#include "cl_util.h"
+#include "parsemsg.h"
+#include "triangleapi.h"
+#include "draw_util.h"
+#include "vgui_parser.h"
+
+#include <stdio.h>
+#include <string>
+#include <vector>
+
+#include "tutor_logic.h"
+#include "client_texture.h"
+#include "text_utf8.h"
+
+static const char *const s_iconFiles[Tutor::ICON_COUNT] =
+{
+	"gfx/career/icon_i.tga",
+	"gfx/career/icon_skulls.tga",
+};
+
+int CHudTutor::Init( void )
+{
+	HOOK_MESSAGE( gHUD.m_Tutor, TutorText );
+	HOOK_MESSAGE( gHUD.m_Tutor, TutorClose );
+	HOOK_MESSAGE( gHUD.m_Tutor, TutorState );
+	HOOK_MESSAGE( gHUD.m_Tutor, TutorLine );
+
+	cl_tutor = CVAR_CREATE( "cl_tutor", "1", FCVAR_ARCHIVE );
+	cl_tutor_maxtime = CVAR_CREATE( "cl_tutor_maxtime", "30", FCVAR_ARCHIVE );
+
+	m_bShow = false;
+	m_iType = Tutor::TYPE_DEFAULT;
+	m_flShownAt = 0.0f;
+	m_bTextAtlas = false;
+	m_iTextW = m_iTextH = 0;
+	m_bTextDirty = false;
+	m_bSchemeLoaded = false;
+
+	for( int i = 0; i < Tutor::ICON_COUNT; ++i )
+	{
+		m_iIconTex[i] = 0;
+		m_bIconTried[i] = false;
+	}
+
+	m_iFlags = HUD_DRAW | HUD_INTERMISSION;
+	gHUD.AddHudElem( this );
+	return 1;
+}
+
+int CHudTutor::VidInit( void )
+{
+	// a new map: the files of the server (scheme, icons) may be other ones
+	Hide();
+	FreeText();
+
+	m_scheme = Tutor::Scheme();
+	m_bSchemeLoaded = false;
+
+	for( int i = 0; i < Tutor::ICON_COUNT; ++i )
+	{
+		m_iIconTex[i] = 0;
+		m_bIconTried[i] = false;
+	}
+
+	return 1;
+}
+
+void CHudTutor::InitHUDData( void )
+{
+	Hide();
+}
+
+void CHudTutor::Hide( void )
+{
+	m_bShow = false;
+	m_szText.clear();
+}
+
+void CHudTutor::FreeText( void )
+{
+	m_text.Free();
+	m_bTextAtlas = false;
+	m_iTextW = m_iTextH = 0;
+	m_lines.clear();
+	m_bTextDirty = true;
+}
+
+// resource/TutorScheme.res and the icons are read when the first message of a map comes:
+// by then the server has sent them
+void CHudTutor::LoadResources( void )
+{
+	if( !m_bSchemeLoaded )
+	{
+		m_bSchemeLoaded = true;
+		m_scheme = Tutor::Scheme();
+
+		int len = 0;
+		byte *data = gEngfuncs.COM_LoadFile( "resource/TutorScheme.res", 5, &len );
+
+		if( data )
+		{
+			const std::string text( (const char *)data, len > 0 ? (size_t)len : 0 );
+			gEngfuncs.COM_FreeFile( data );
+			Tutor::ParseScheme( text.c_str(), m_scheme );
+		}
+	}
+
+	for( int i = 0; i < Tutor::ICON_COUNT; ++i )
+	{
+		if( m_iIconTex[i] > 0 || m_bIconTried[i] || !gRenderAPI.GL_LoadTexture )
+			continue;
+
+		m_bIconTried[i] = true;
+
+		// the engine prints nothing if there is no such file: the client then draws the icon itself
+		if( gEngfuncs.COM_LoadFile )
+		{
+			int len = 0;
+			byte *probe = gEngfuncs.COM_LoadFile( s_iconFiles[i], 5, &len );
+
+			if( !probe )
+				continue;
+
+			gEngfuncs.COM_FreeFile( probe );
+		}
+
+		m_iIconTex[i] = gRenderAPI.GL_LoadTexture( s_iconFiles[i], NULL, 0, TF_NOMIPMAP | TF_CLAMP );
+	}
+}
+
+int CHudTutor::MsgFunc_TutorText( const char *pszName, int iSize, void *pbuf )
+{
+	BufferReader reader( pszName, pbuf, iSize );
+
+	// the strings are copied at once: the reader gives all of them in one buffer
+	const std::string raw = reader.ReadString();
+	const int numArgs = reader.ReadByte();
+	std::vector<std::string> args;
+
+	for( int i = 0; i < numArgs; ++i )
+	{
+		const std::string arg = reader.ReadString();
+
+		if( i < 9 )
+			args.push_back( TextUtf::ToUtf8( arg.c_str() ));
+	}
+
+	reader.ReadShort(); // number of the message in tutordata.txt
+	reader.ReadShort(); // the player is dead
+	const int type = reader.ReadShort();
+
+	// "#Key" is a string of the game (resource/cstrike_<language>.txt)
+	const char *text = raw.c_str();
+
+	if( text[0] == '#' )
+		text = Localize( text );
+
+	const std::string message = Tutor::CleanText( Tutor::Substitute( TextUtf::ToUtf8( text ), args ));
+
+	if( message.empty() )
+	{
+		Hide();
+		return 1;
+	}
+
+	LoadResources();
+
+	if( message != m_szText )
+	{
+		m_szText = message;
+		FreeText();
+	}
+
+	m_iType = type > 0 ? type : Tutor::TYPE_DEFAULT;
+	m_flShownAt = gHUD.m_flTime;
+	m_bShow = true;
+
+	if( gEngfuncs.pfnGetCvarFloat( "developer" ) > 0 )
+		gEngfuncs.Con_Printf( "[tutor] type %d: %s\n", m_iType, m_szText.c_str() );
+
+	return 1;
+}
+
+int CHudTutor::MsgFunc_TutorClose( const char *pszName, int iSize, void *pbuf )
+{
+	Hide();
+	return 1;
+}
+
+int CHudTutor::MsgFunc_TutorState( const char *pszName, int iSize, void *pbuf )
+{
+	// the state of the tutor of Condition Zero, not shown in CS 1.6
+	BufferReader reader( pszName, pbuf, iSize );
+	reader.ReadString();
+	return 1;
+}
+
+int CHudTutor::MsgFunc_TutorLine( const char *pszName, int iSize, void *pbuf )
+{
+	// a line to an entity, not used by the game
+	return 1;
+}
+
+// The picture of the text (Windows fonts) or its lines for the font of the HUD; maxWidth - the widest line
+void CHudTutor::BuildText( int maxWidth )
+{
+	m_bTextDirty = false;
+
+	// the text is in screen pixels, the layout is in the units of the HUD (the same unless hud_scale is used)
+	const float scale = gHUD.m_flScale > 0.0f ? gHUD.m_flScale : 1.0f;
+
+	if( m_text.Update( m_szText, m_scheme.fontName.c_str(), (int)( Tutor::FontEmHeight( m_scheme.fontTall ) * scale + 0.5f ),
+			m_scheme.fontWeight, m_scheme.fontAntialias, (int)( maxWidth * scale )) && m_text.Valid() )
+	{
+		m_bTextAtlas = true;
+		m_iTextW = m_text.Width();
+		m_iTextH = m_text.Height();
+		return;
+	}
+	m_bTextAtlas = false;
+
+	// no Windows fonts: the font of the HUD
+	m_lines = Tutor::ClipLines( m_szText, maxWidth, []( const std::string &s ) { return DrawUtils::HudStringLen( s.c_str() ); } );
+	m_iTextW = 0;
+
+	for( const std::string &line : m_lines )
+	{
+		const int lw = DrawUtils::HudStringLen( line.c_str() );
+		if( lw > m_iTextW )
+			m_iTextW = lw;
+	}
+
+	m_iTextH = (int)m_lines.size() * gHUD.GetCharHeight();
+}
+
+static void DrawTexture( int tex, float x, float y, float w, float h, const Tutor::Color &c, float scale )
+{
+	gRenderAPI.GL_SelectTexture( 0 );
+	gRenderAPI.GL_Bind( 0, tex );
+	gEngfuncs.pTriAPI->RenderMode( kRenderTransAlpha );
+	gEngfuncs.pTriAPI->Color4f( c.r / 255.0f, c.g / 255.0f, c.b / 255.0f, c.a / 255.0f );
+	DrawUtils::Draw2DQuad( x * scale, y * scale, ( x + w ) * scale, ( y + h ) * scale );
+}
+
+// The icon drawn by the client when the server did not send gfx/career/*.tga:
+// a rounded square of the colour of the message with a dark sign on it
+static void DrawOwnIcon( int x, int y, Tutor::Icon icon, const Tutor::Color &c )
+{
+	const int s = Tutor::Size::IconSize - 2;
+	x += 1;
+	y += 1;
+
+	DrawUtils::FillRoundedRect( x, y, s, s, 3, true, true, c.r, c.g, c.b, 255 );
+
+	if( icon == Tutor::ICON_SKULL )
+	{
+		// a cross
+		const int n = s - 12;
+
+		for( int i = 0; i < n; ++i )
+		{
+			FillRGBA( x + 6 + i, y + 6 + i, 2, 2, 20, 20, 20, 255 );
+			FillRGBA( x + s - 8 - i, y + 6 + i, 2, 2, 20, 20, 20, 255 );
+		}
+	}
+	else
+	{
+		// "i"
+		const int cx = x + s / 2;
+		FillRGBA( cx - 2, y + 4, 4, 3, 20, 20, 20, 255 );
+		FillRGBA( cx - 2, y + 9, 4, s - 13, 20, 20, 20, 255 );
+	}
+}
+
+int CHudTutor::Draw( float flTime )
+{
+	if( !m_bShow || m_szText.empty() )
+		return 1;
+
+	if( cl_tutor && cl_tutor->value == 0.0f )
+		return 1;
+
+	// the server forgot to close it (or its TutorClose was lost)
+	if( cl_tutor_maxtime && cl_tutor_maxtime->value > 0.0f && flTime - m_flShownAt > cl_tutor_maxtime->value )
+	{
+		Hide();
+		return 1;
+	}
+
+	// a new map started: the time of the client starts from zero again
+	if( flTime < m_flShownAt )
+		m_flShownAt = flTime;
+
+	const float scale = gHUD.m_flScale > 0.0f ? gHUD.m_flScale : 1.0f;
+
+	if( m_bTextDirty )
+		BuildText( Tutor::MaxTextWidth( ScreenWidth ));
+
+	// in units of the HUD
+	const int textW = m_bTextAtlas ? (int)( m_iTextW / scale + 0.5f ) : m_iTextW;
+	const int textH = m_bTextAtlas ? (int)( m_iTextH / scale + 0.5f ) : m_iTextH;
+
+	// in the spectator mode the window is below the upper bar of the spectator
+	int top = 0;
+	if( g_iUser1 && gHUD.GetGameType() != GAME_CZERODS )
+		top = CHudSpectatorGui::BarHeight();
+
+	const Tutor::Layout l = Tutor::ComputeLayout( ScreenWidth, top, textW, textH );
+	const Tutor::Color bg = m_scheme.background;
+	const Tutor::Color color = m_scheme.ColorForType( m_iType );
+	const Tutor::Icon icon = Tutor::IconForType( m_iType );
+
+	// the panel: the part with the icon and the part with the text, the game is seen through the cut between them
+	const int rightX = l.cutX + Tutor::Size::Cut;
+	DrawUtils::FillRoundedRectSides( l.x, l.y, l.cutX - l.x, l.h, Tutor::Size::Radius, true, false, bg.r, bg.g, bg.b, bg.a );
+	DrawUtils::FillRoundedRectSides( rightX, l.y, l.x + l.w - rightX, l.h, Tutor::Size::Radius, false, true, bg.r, bg.g, bg.b, bg.a );
+
+	// the icon: a white picture painted with the colour of the message
+	if( m_iIconTex[icon] > 0 )
+	{
+		const Tutor::Color opaque = { color.r, color.g, color.b, 255 };
+		DrawTexture( m_iIconTex[icon], (float)l.iconX, (float)l.iconY, (float)Tutor::Size::IconSize, (float)Tutor::Size::IconSize, opaque, scale );
+	}
+	else
+	{
+		DrawOwnIcon( l.iconX, l.iconY, icon, color );
+	}
+
+	// the text
+	if( m_bTextAtlas )
+	{
+		m_text.Draw( l.textX * scale, l.textY * scale, color.r, color.g, color.b, color.a );
+	}
+	else
+	{
+		int y = l.textY;
+
+		for( const std::string &line : m_lines )
+		{
+			DrawUtils::DrawHudString( l.textX, y, ScreenWidth, line.c_str(), color.r, color.g, color.b );
+			y += gHUD.GetCharHeight();
+		}
+	}
+
+	gEngfuncs.pTriAPI->RenderMode( kRenderNormal );
+	return 1;
+}
diff --git a/cl_dll/hud/tutor_logic.h b/cl_dll/hud/tutor_logic.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0299152
--- /dev/null
+++ b/cl_dll/hud/tutor_logic.h
@@ -0,0 +1,452 @@
+//
+// tutor_logic.h
+//
+// Tutor messages of the server (TutorText / TutorClose / TutorState / TutorLine, as sent by ReGameDLL
+// and by AMX Mod X plugins): the colours and the font from resource/TutorScheme.res, the text with its
+// parameters and the layout of the window.
+// No dependencies on the engine, so it can be tested alone.
+//
+// The window is the one of the Steam version, measured on its screenshots (1920x1080); the sizes are
+// the ones of resource/UI/TutorTextWindow.res and do not depend on the resolution:
+//  - in the upper right corner, 10 pixels from the right and from the top
+//    (10 pixels below the upper bar of the spectator mode when it is shown);
+//  - a dark rounded panel (radius 10), 45 pixels high for one line of text;
+//  - on the left a part 40 pixels wide with the icon 25x25 at (10, 10), then a cut of 2 pixels
+//    through which the game is seen, then the text from x = 50 with 17 pixels on the right;
+//  - the text is in one line (the Steam version does not wrap it, the window just gets wider),
+//    Tahoma 14 of the scheme drawn 10 pixels high (em), not antialiased, in the colour of the type.
+//
+
+#pragma once
+
+#include <stddef.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
+#include <string>
+#include <vector>
+
+namespace Tutor {
+
+// Types of messages (ReGameDLL, tutor_cs_tutor.h): the server sends one of these bits
+enum
+{
+	TYPE_DEFAULT      = 1 << 0, // info, green
+	TYPE_FRIEND_DEATH = 1 << 1, // skull, red
+	TYPE_ENEMY_DEATH  = 1 << 2, // skull, blue
+	TYPE_SCENARIO     = 1 << 3, // info, yellow
+	TYPE_BUY          = 1 << 4,
+	TYPE_CAREER       = 1 << 5,
+	TYPE_HINT         = 1 << 6,
+	TYPE_INGAME_HINT  = 1 << 7,
+	TYPE_END_GAME     = 1 << 8, // info, yellow
+};
+
+enum Icon
+{
+	ICON_INFO = 0,
+	ICON_SKULL,
+	ICON_COUNT
+};
+
+struct Color
+{
+	unsigned char r, g, b, a;
+};
+
+inline bool SameColor( const Color& x, const Color& y )
+{
+	return x.r == y.r && x.g == y.g && x.b == y.b && x.a == y.a;
+}
+
+// What the window looks like (defaults are the values of TutorScheme.res of the Steam version)
+struct Scheme
+{
+	Color background = { 0, 0, 0, 200 };       // "WindowBG"
+	Color classDefault = { 28, 207, 61, 255 };   // "TutorTextClassDefault"
+
+	struct ClassColor
+	{
+		int type;
+		Color color;
+	};
+	std::vector<ClassColor> classes = {
+		{ TYPE_FRIEND_DEATH, { 255, 38, 38, 255 } },  // "TutorTextClass2"
+		{ TYPE_ENEMY_DEATH,  { 38, 149, 253, 255 } }, // "TutorTextClass4"
+		{ TYPE_SCENARIO,     { 255, 227, 38, 255 } }, // "TutorTextClass8"
+		{ TYPE_END_GAME,     { 255, 227, 38, 255 } }, // "TutorTextClass256"
+	};
+
+	std::string fontName = "Tahoma"; // Fonts / "Default" / "1"
+	int fontTall = 14;
+	int fontWeight = 500;
+	bool fontAntialias = false;
+
+	void SetClassColor( int type, const Color& c )
+	{
+		for( ClassColor& cc : classes )
+		{
+			if( cc.type == type )
+			{
+				cc.color = c;
+				return;
+			}
+		}
+
+		classes.push_back( { type, c } );
+	}
+
+	Color ColorForType( int type ) const
+	{
+		for( const ClassColor& cc : classes )
+			if( cc.type == type )
+				return cc.color;
+
+		return classDefault;
+	}
+};
+
+inline Icon IconForType( int type )
+{
+	return ( type == TYPE_FRIEND_DEATH || type == TYPE_ENEMY_DEATH ) ? ICON_SKULL : ICON_INFO;
+}
+
+// ---- reading of resource/TutorScheme.res (the KeyValues format of the Valve resource files)
+
+namespace detail {
+
+inline bool IsSpace( char c )
+{
+	return c == ' ' || c == '\t' || c == '\r' || c == '\n';
+}
+
+// Next token: a quoted string, '{', '}' or a bare word. Comments (//) are skipped. Returns false at the end.
+inline bool NextToken( const char*& p, std::string& token, bool& quoted )
+{
+	for( ;; )
+	{
+		while( *p && IsSpace( *p ))
+			p++;
+
+		if( p[0] == '/' && p[1] == '/' )
+		{
+			while( *p && *p != '\n' )
+				p++;
+			continue;
+		}
+
+		break;
+	}
+
+	if( !*p )
+		return false;
+
+	token.clear();
+	quoted = false;
+
+	if( *p == '{' || *p == '}' )
+	{
+		token = *p++;
+		return true;
+	}
+
+	if( *p == '"' )
+	{
+		quoted = true;
+		p++;
+
+		while( *p && *p != '"' && token.size() < 1024 )
+			token += *p++;
+
+		if( *p == '"' )
+			p++;
+
+		return true;
+	}
+
+	while( *p && !IsSpace( *p ) && *p != '{' && *p != '}' && *p != '"' && token.size() < 1024 )
+		token += *p++;
+
+	return true;
+}
+
+inline std::string Lower( std::string s )
+{
+	for( char& c : s )
+		if( c >= 'A' && c <= 'Z' )
+			c = (char)( c - 'A' + 'a' );
+	return s;
+}
+
+inline bool ParseColor( const std::string& s, Color& out )
+{
+	int v[4] = { 0, 0, 0, 255 };
+	int n = 0;
+	const char* p = s.c_str();
+
+	while( n < 4 )
+	{
+		char *end = nullptr;
+		const long x = strtol( p, &end, 10 );
+
+		if( end == p )
+			break;
+
+		v[n++] = x < -1000 ? -1000 : ( x > 1000 ? 1000 : (int)x );
+		p = end;
+	}
+
+	if( n < 3 )
+		return false;
+
+	for( int& x : v )
+		x = x < 0 ? 0 : ( x > 255 ? 255 : x );
+
+	out = { (unsigned char)v[0], (unsigned char)v[1], (unsigned char)v[2], (unsigned char)v[3] };
+	return true;
+}
+
+} // namespace detail
+
+// Takes from the text of TutorScheme.res what the window uses: the colours of the background and of the
+// types of the messages, and the first font of "Default". Everything else is kept as it is in the scheme.
+// Values that are missing or wrong keep their defaults.
+inline void ParseScheme( const char* text, Scheme& scheme )
+{
+	if( !text )
+		return;
+
+	using namespace detail;
+
+	std::vector<std::string> path; // the sections we are in, in lower case
+	std::string token, key;
+	bool quoted = false;
+	bool haveKey = false;
+	bool fontTaken = false;
+	const char* p = text;
+
+	while( NextToken( p, token, quoted ))
+	{
+		if( !quoted && token == "{" )
+		{
+			path.push_back( haveKey ? Lower( key ) : std::string());
+			haveKey = false;
+			continue;
+		}
+
+		if( !quoted && token == "}" )
+		{
+			if( !path.empty() )
+			{
+				// the end of the first font of "Default": the next ones are only fallbacks
+				if( path.size() >= 4 && path[1] == "fonts" && path[2] == "default" )
+					fontTaken = true;
+				path.pop_back();
+			}
+			haveKey = false;
+			continue;
+		}
+
+		if( !haveKey )
+		{
+			key = token;
+			haveKey = true;
+			continue;
+		}
+
+		// key + value
+		const std::string lk = Lower( key );
+		haveKey = false;
+
+		if( path.size() == 2 && path[1] == "colors" )
+		{
+			Color c;
+
+			if( !ParseColor( token, c ))
+				continue;
+
+			if( lk == "windowbg" )
+				scheme.background = c;
+			else if( lk == "tutortextclassdefault" )
+				scheme.classDefault = c;
+			else if( lk.compare( 0, 14, "tutortextclass" ) == 0 && lk.size() > 14 && lk[14] >= '0' && lk[14] <= '9' )
+				scheme.SetClassColor( atoi( lk.c_str() + 14 ), c );
+		}
+		else if( path.size() == 4 && path[1] == "fonts" && path[2] == "default" && !fontTaken )
+		{
+			if( lk == "name" && !token.empty() && token.size() < 32 )
+				scheme.fontName = token;
+			else if( lk == "tall" )
+			{
+				const int t = atoi( token.c_str() );
+				if( t >= 6 && t <= 48 )
+					scheme.fontTall = t;
+			}
+			else if( lk == "weight" )
+			{
+				const int w = atoi( token.c_str() );
+				if( w >= 100 && w <= 900 )
+					scheme.fontWeight = w;
+			}
+			else if( lk == "antialias" )
+				scheme.fontAntialias = atoi( token.c_str() ) != 0;
+		}
+	}
+}
+
+// ---- the text
+
+// Puts the parameters of the message into its text: %s1 .. %s9 (as the Steam version does)
+inline std::string Substitute( const std::string& text, const std::vector<std::string>& args )
+{
+	std::string out;
+	out.reserve( text.size() );
+
+	for( size_t i = 0; i < text.size(); )
+	{
+		if( text[i] == '%' && i + 2 < text.size() && text[i + 1] == 's' && text[i + 2] >= '1' && text[i + 2] <= '9' )
+		{
+			const size_t idx = (size_t)( text[i + 2] - '1' );
+
+			if( idx < args.size() )
+				out += args[idx];
+
+			i += 3;
+			continue;
+		}
+
+		out += text[i++];
+	}
+
+	return out;
+}
+
+// The text is made ready to be drawn: Windows line ends and the line ends at the end are removed,
+// control characters other than line ends become spaces
+inline std::string CleanText( const std::string& text )
+{
+	std::string out;
+	out.reserve( text.size() );
+
+	for( char c : text )
+	{
+		if( c == '\r' )
+			continue;
+
+		if( (unsigned char)c < ' ' && c != '\n' )
+			c = ' ';
+
+		out += c;
+	}
+
+	while( !out.empty() && ( out.back() == '\n' || out.back() == ' ' ))
+		out.pop_back();
+
+	return out;
+}
+
+// ---- the layout
+
+namespace Size {
+const int Margin = 10;      // from the right edge and from the top of the screen (or of the spectator bar)
+const int Radius = 10;
+const int MinHeight = 45;
+const int LeftWidth = 40;   // the part with the icon
+const int Cut = 2;          // the cut between the parts
+const int IconPos = 10;
+const int IconSize = 25;
+const int TextX = 50;       // the text starts here
+const int TextRight = 17;   // room on the right of the text
+const int TextPad = 10;     // room above and below the text when it has many lines (line ends in the text)
+} // namespace Size
+
+// The Steam version draws the "tall" of a scheme with letters of tall * 3 / 4 pixels (rounded down, the em):
+// the tutor font ("tall" 14) has letters of 10 pixels, capitals of 7 and small letters of 5 (measured on its
+// screenshots; the font of the spectator bar gives the same rule, see spectator_layout.h)
+inline int FontEmHeight( int schemeTall )
+{
+	const int em = schemeTall * 3 / 4;
+	return em < 4 ? 4 : em;
+}
+
+struct Layout
+{
+	int x = 0, y = 0, w = 0, h = 0;  // the panel
+	int iconX = 0, iconY = 0;
+	int cutX = 0;                    // the cut is cutX .. cutX + Size::Cut
+	int textX = 0, textY = 0;
+};
+
+// The longest line that fits on the screen (a longer one is cut at the right edge of the window)
+inline int MaxTextWidth( int screenW )
+{
+	int w = screenW - Size::Margin - Size::TextX - Size::TextRight;
+	if( w < 50 )
+		w = 50;
+	return w;
+}
+
+// screenW - width of the screen, top - where the window may start (0, or the bottom of the spectator bar),
+// textW / textH - the size of the drawn text
+inline Layout ComputeLayout( int screenW, int top, int textW, int textH )
+{
+	Layout l;
+
+	if( textW < 0 ) textW = 0;
+	if( textH < 0 ) textH = 0;
+
+	l.w = Size::TextX + textW + Size::TextRight;
+	l.h = textH + Size::TextPad * 2;
+	if( l.h < Size::MinHeight )
+		l.h = Size::MinHeight;
+
+	l.x = screenW - Size::Margin - l.w;
+	if( l.x < 0 )
+		l.x = 0;
+	l.y = top + Size::Margin;
+
+	l.iconX = l.x + Size::IconPos;
+	l.iconY = l.y + Size::IconPos;
+	l.cutX = l.x + Size::LeftWidth;
+	l.textX = l.x + Size::TextX;
+
+	// in the middle of the panel, as in the Steam version
+	l.textY = l.y + ( l.h - textH ) / 2;
+
+	return l;
+}
+
+// The text split at its line ends; a line wider than maxWidth is cut (UTF-8 letters are kept whole).
+// For the font of the HUD (the Windows fonts cut the lines by themselves).
+// width( const std::string& ) gives the width of a piece of text.
+template <class WidthFn>
+std::vector<std::string> ClipLines( const std::string& text, int maxWidth, WidthFn width )
+{
+	std::vector<std::string> lines;
+	size_t start = 0;
+
+	for( ;; )
+	{
+		const size_t end = text.find( '\n', start );
+		std::string line = text.substr( start, end == std::string::npos ? std::string::npos : end - start );
+
+		while( !line.empty() && width( line ) > maxWidth )
+		{
+			size_t cut = line.size() - 1;
+
+			while( cut > 0 && ( (unsigned char)line[cut] & 0xC0 ) == 0x80 )
+				--cut;
+
+			line.erase( cut );
+		}
+
+		lines.push_back( line );
+
+		if( end == std::string::npos )
+			break;
+		start = end + 1;
+	}
+
+	return lines;
+}
+
+} // namespace Tutor
